    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable. The fee stands or falls on POL-NS-01, which needs all four of its conditions. Two are met. The driver did arrive: the GPS trace EV-GPS-00203 (weight 1.0) shows 21 consecutive qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius with the closest approach 18.7 m, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied and limb (b) holds. The trip record EV-TRIP-00203 (weight 1.0) records a driver cancellation with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, as limb (d) requires. But the case fails on the arithmetic of limb (c). Measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 19:41:20 and not from the 'arrived' tap, the driver's longest continuous in-geofence dwell was 195 seconds (EV-GPS-00203) against the 300-second STANDARD minimum in POL-NS-01 limb (c) - a shortfall of 105 seconds. Limb (d) fails with it, because the trip was terminated at 19:44:40, before the five minutes could run out (the clock would not have expired until 19:46:20); the trip record's own wait_time_min of 3.1 minutes is the driver's own record of the abbreviated wait. POL-NS-06 then decides the money, and it is strict: where the effective in-geofence dwell falls short of the minimum the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider answered messages. The sum to return is the cancellation-fee line only - SGD 4.00, shown as CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 in EV-FARE-00203 (weight 1.0), which reconciles with the fee schedule because the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee are both SGD 4.00, the greater-of rule producing SGD 4.00 with no integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d). The driver's points are accepted. The arrival marker was not false: at the 19:41:35 'arrived' event the driver was stationary inside the 50 m radius, 15 seconds into his in-geofence run, so neither POL-NS-05 trigger (more than 300 m from the pin, or travelling at 15 km/h or more) is met and no false-arrival referral arises against him under POL-NS-05(ii). The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) cannot rescue the fee: there is only one in-geofence interval (run_count 1), and limb (i) also requires a present and populated traffic advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT - EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so the limb is unavailable rather than satisfied. POL-NS-04 is not the route to this refund: the driver replied to the rider's 19:42:50 message at 19:44:31, 101 seconds later and inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) of that clause fails and the clause does not apply; the refund rests on the dwell shortfall, not on rider contact. The rider's presence is not in dispute - all 60 rider fixes sit between 36.4 m and 51.6 m of the pin (mean 42.8 m), inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius - but the outcome does not depend on it. The chat log EV-CHAT-00203 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 with issue LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY; it corroborates that the driver cancelled as the rider was asking him to wait ('cannot wait already ah, cancelling' at 19:44:31, nine seconds before the 19:44:40 cancellation), but the cancellation timestamp it shows is independently carried by the weight-1.0 trip record, so no part of this ruling rests on the impaired artifact and the finding survives the discount. No driver compensation: POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and here limb (c) fails and POL-NS-06 applies directly, so the SGD 3.20 in the fare breakdown's derived money block is not owed and the SGD 4.00 belongs to the rider. The figures used are the 195-second dwell, the 300-second STANDARD minimum, the 105-second shortfall and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee. Confidence is 0.90: the deciding facts are carried by the weight-1.0 GPS trace, trip record and fare breakdown, and no artifact that decides the case is impaired. No referral is produced - no clause in this category directs one on these facts."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver cannot repair the shortfall by accumulating separate in-geofence intervals under POL-NS-06(i). There is only one in-geofence interval in the trace — a single 21-fix qualifying run, run_count 1 — so there is no second interval for the limb to add. The limb also requires a present and populated traffic_advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covering the pickup road, and none exists: EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING with weight 0.00, and under POL-GEN-02 a missing artifact carries no fact and can only be cited as an absence. Limb (i) is therefore unavailable and the 105 second shortfall stands untouched.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00203-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
